From d6d3fe2f9dfa6410aab468cb30ba20f3028062c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rob Paprocki <hi@rpaprocki.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 00:48:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06/29] security: remove the inbound callback endpoints of the
 push model

GitHub runners no longer call back into rdgen, so these are gone:

  /get_zip             served the encrypted config (upstream fixed only its
                       traversal, in 3d098ab)
  /get_png             served uploaded images; had the same
                       os.path.join traversal as /download
                       (?filename=/proc/self/environ)
  /save_custom_client  unauthenticated multipart upload; uuid=../x wrote
                       files anywhere the service could write
  /cleanzip            unauthenticated delete; never matched the zip name
                       anyway (secrets_<new uuid4>.zip vs build uuid)
  /updategh            unauthenticated status write; nothing sent it any
                       more
  /startgh             unauthenticated proxy that dispatched workflows with
                       the PAT and concatenated user input into the API URL
  /creategh            a helper function mapped as a view

Also dropped the unused helpers (save_png, resize_and_encode_icon) and
the imports they needed.

